# Soft deploy

A production update builds while the current process keeps answering. Do not restart the service until a standby copy of the new build is already answering. The edge uses that standby when the main port refuses a connection, so the restart does not answer 502.

## Order

1. Pull and build. Leave the service running.
2. Start the standby. Wait until it returns 200.
3. If the standby never answers, stop it and leave the service as it is.
4. Restart the service only after the standby answers.
5. Wait until the service answers 200 again, then stop the standby.

Do not restart the service first. Do not restart the other sites on that machine. Host, ports, the standby command, and the nginx upstream are in `.cursor/skills/trenio-vps/SKILL.md`. Do not copy them into this rule, and do not print `.env`.
